\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Pipeline version 2 (US-017). The saturation lerp runs first so the grayscale luminance is computed from the un-degraded source. Additive noise and salt-and-pepper operate at the pre-upsample resolution; bicubic upsample spreads each stochastic sample over the kernel footprint, producing sensor-grain noise structure rather than fine pixel-level grain.}}{6}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{2}{6}{Pipeline version 2 (US-017). The saturation lerp runs first so the grayscale luminance is computed from the un-degraded source. Additive noise and salt-and-pepper operate at the pre-upsample resolution; bicubic upsample spreads each stochastic sample over the kernel footprint, producing sensor-grain noise structure rather than fine pixel-level grain}{figure.caption.9}{}}
